{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1124","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1124","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1124\",\"parent_revision\":\"d04e5b702cc425b4ec25c1ad033f2b17b4658308\",\"root_revision\":\"41d0424d1a025ba740eff9a5f95564913568cd15e6e194b27b08cffb6a56d3df\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nQuality gate commands support `{files}` template variable substitution per the manifest schema contract, but `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py` has zero tests for a command containing `{files}`.\\n\\nSuggested test: `test_run_quality_gates_when_command_contains_files_template_then_variable_handled`\\n\\nThis is a documented contract between the manifest schema and the gate runner. Without this test, silent regression in `{files}` substitution would pass CI.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA SUMMARY\\n\\nGoal:\\n- Add a test that verifies `run_quality_gates` correctly handles a command containing the `{files}` template variable, so that silent regression in `{files}` substitution fails CI.\\n\\nSuccess Output:\\n- A new test class or test function in `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py` that passes under `uv run pytest`.\\n\\nConditions (reverse prerequisites):\\n1. `{files}` substitution exists in the gate runner | Requires: code path in `gates.py` or caller | Why: Can only test a mechanism that is implemented\\n2. Test follows the file's AAA/naming/mock conventions | Requires: existing test file patterns | Why: Consistency and review compliance\\n3. Reproduction command executable locally | Requires: `dispatch_schema` installed in dev environment | Why: Validate test pass/fail before committing\\n\\nVerification:\\n- `{files}` substitution in gate runner: MISSING | The current `gates.py` has NO `{files}` substitution logic \u2014 `run_quality_gates` executes commands verbatim via `shlex.split`. The `{files}` placeholder is a schema-level convention documented for callers/agents (see `language-manifest-schema.md`, `poc-validation-guide.md`, `generic-stage-agent.md`), but substitution is the caller's responsibility before passing commands to `run_quality_gates`.\\n- Test conventions: AVAILABLE | `test_gates.py` has complete AAA patterns, `MockerFixture`, `_make_completed_process`, class grouping.\\n- Reproduction command: AVAILABLE | `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py`\\n\\nDecision:\\n- BLOCKED \u2014 the implementation question must be resolved before the test can be written.\\n\\nMissing Inputs Requested:\\n\\nBehavior scope:\\n- Does `run_quality_gates` itself perform `{files}` substitution, or is that always the caller's responsibility? If the gate runner is NOT expected to substitute, the contract is that callers pre-expand `{files}` before calling `run_quality_gates` \u2014 and the test should verify that a literal `{files}` in a command string is passed through unchanged (no substitution in the runner). If the gate runner IS expected to substitute, then `gates.py` is missing an implementation and needs both an implementation commit and a test.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-29T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-03-29T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **add missing coverage for {files} template variable in run_quality_gates** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Test quality audit 2026-03-29\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-03-30)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Navigate to `/home/user/claude_skills`.\\n2. Run `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py -v`.\\n3. Observe: no test covers a command string containing `{files}`. The absence is visible by grepping the file: `grep -n 'files' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py` returns zero matches.\\n\\n### Output / Evidence\\n\\n- `grep -n 'files' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py` \u2014 returns no output, confirming zero coverage.\\n- `grep -rn 'files' plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/gates.py` \u2014 also returns no output, confirming the gate runner itself has no `{files}` substitution logic.\\n- Documentation references in `language-manifest-schema.md:70`, `poc-validation-guide.md:183-184`, and `generic-stage-agent.md:20` describe the `{files}` contract as caller-side substitution.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n6/10 \u2014 Documented schema contract with zero test coverage is a real regression risk. Deprioritised slightly because the RT-ICA assessment reveals an open implementation question: if `run_quality_gates` is not responsible for substitution (current code confirms this), the test is a contract-documentation test rather than a functional regression guard.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: Any future refactor of `gates.py` that accidentally introduces or breaks `{files}` handling would not be caught by CI.\\n- Bottleneck: The `{files}` template is used in every language manifest (Python, TypeScript, Bash, Perl examples in `language-manifest-schema.md`). A silent regression affects all gate runs that use format/lint/typecheck commands.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- Locks down the `{files}` pass-through contract in `run_quality_gates`, preventing future regressions.\\n- Provides executable documentation that the gate runner does NOT substitute `{files}` (callers must pre-expand).\\n- Consistent with the existing test module's thoroughness (127/timeout/cwd/mode coverage).\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen `run_quality_gates` receives a command string containing `{files}` (e.g., `\\\"uv run ruff check {files}\\\"`), it executes the command as-is \u2014 `{files}` is passed verbatim to `shlex.split` and then to `subprocess.run`. The gate runner does not perform string substitution. Callers are responsible for expanding `{files}` before calling `run_quality_gates`.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nA new test class `TestFilesTemplateVariable` (or equivalent) in `test_gates.py` containing at least one test that verifies the observable behaviour of `run_quality_gates` when the command contains `{files}`. The test must use `MockerFixture`, follow the file's AAA layout, and name itself `test_run_quality_gates_when_command_contains_files_template_then_variable_handled` (or split into focused single-assertion tests per the file's convention).\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. `grep -n 'files' plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py` returns at least one match in a test function or class.\\n2. `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py -v` exits 0 with the new test shown as PASSED.\\n3. The new test verifies observable behaviour only \u2014 it asserts on the `subprocess.run` call args or on `CommandResult` fields, not on internal implementation details.\\n4. The test uses `MockerFixture` (no `unittest.mock` imports).\\n5. `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py` exits 0 (linting clean).\\n\\n### Human Input\\n\\nThe key ambiguity flagged by RT-ICA: does `run_quality_gates` substitute `{files}`, or is that always the caller's responsibility?\\n\\nReading `gates.py` directly: the gate runner does NOT substitute `{files}`. The function calls `shlex.split(command)` on the raw string and executes it. There is no `.format()` or template expansion.\\n\\nThe `{files}` contract is documented as caller-side in `poc-validation-guide.md:183-184`, `generic-stage-agent.md:20`, and `scripts/dispatch_helper.py:120-121`.\\n\\nConclusion: the test should assert pass-through behaviour \u2014 that a command containing `{files}` is executed verbatim, with `{files}` appearing literally in the `subprocess.run` call args. If the intent is different (i.e., the runner should substitute), please confirm before implementing.\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Is `run_quality_gates` expected to perform `{files}` substitution internally, or is the documented contract that callers always pre-expand `{files}` before calling the function?\\n- If callers pre-expand: the test should verify pass-through (literal `{files}` in tokens). If the runner should expand: `gates.py` needs an implementation change first, and the test is a regression guard for that new behaviour.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Implementation | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/dispatch_schema/gates.py` |\\n| Test file | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/test_gates.py` |\\n| Test fixtures | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/tests/test_dispatch_schema/conftest.py` |\\n| Schema contract docs | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/development-harness/references/language-manifest-schema.md:60-71` |\\n| Agent contract | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/agents/generic-stage-agent.md:20` |\\n| POC validation guide | `/home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/docs/poc-validation-guide.md:183-184` |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None (test file and gates.py are self-contained).\\n- Blocks: None identified in the current backlog.\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- RT-ICA BLOCKED: the intended behaviour of `run_quality_gates` when given a `{files}` command is not explicitly documented in the function's docstring or in the test file's module docstring. The observable code shows pass-through behaviour (no substitution), but whether this is the intended contract or an oversight requires confirmation before writing a passing test.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 `gates.py` is 104 lines, `test_gates.py` is 850 lines with clear class-based grouping. Adding one test class with 2-3 focused tests follows established patterns directly. Once the behaviour question is resolved, implementation is under 1 hour.\\n\",\"digest\":\"2de3a8541c22880fb887789ca06213a70b9809eeaea319f23072987e0062752c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnH8qQ\"}"}